# Verify Cloudflare CI after push

Pushing `main` on `alxgntv/seenshot-web` deploys production Worker `seenshot-web` to `https://seenshot.app`.

After every `git push` to that branch:

1. Run `gh run list --repo alxgntv/seenshot-web --branch main --limit 5`.
2. Watch the latest `Deploy seenshot.app` run until it finishes (`gh run watch <id> --repo alxgntv/seenshot-web --exit-status`).
3. On success, `curl -sS -o /tmp/seenshot-prod.html -w "%{http_code}" https://seenshot.app/` must be 200 and the HTML must contain `SeenShot`.
4. On failure, `gh run view <id> --log --repo alxgntv/seenshot-web`. Find the root cause. Fix the code. Commit. Push. Watch again. Repeat until the run is green and production curl passes.
5. A green local `vinext` build is not production. Production is that GitHub Actions run.

Do not run `wrangler deploy` or `vinext-cloudflare deploy` from the laptop unless the user explicitly asks for a local deploy. The production path is git push to `main`.
